cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper. If you use the clinical scenarios, you must also cite the MTS-Dialog corpus they are derived from (see the references below and docs/THIRD_PARTY.md)."
title: "Style Without Erasure: Measuring and Removing Speaker-Style Sensitivity in Language Models"
abstract: >-
  A controlled protocol for measuring how a language model's output
  distribution changes when speaker-style cues change while propositional
  content is held byte-identical, and a distribution-preserving intervention
  that removes the behavioural effect. Each style contrast is paired with a
  placebo contrast matched on exact token length and on distance in the
  model's input-embedding space, and every divergence is reported as a share
  of a positive control that replaces the entire propositional content. The
  intervention is self-distillation against a style-blind teacher: a frozen
  base model reading the cue-free prompt supervises a LoRA-adapted student
  reading the cue-present prompt. Behavioural sensitivity to speaker style
  falls substantially while style information remains linearly decodable at
  the resolution the design can measure. Experiments use a single model,
  Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct.
type: software
authors:
